From: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: re-trigger the JCPLL VCO band search on the AN7581 ETH lane

On the AN7581 ETH SerDes lane the JCPLL VCO band search runs only once, from
an7581_pcs_jcpll_bringup(), and it programs JCPLL_VCO_TCLVAR *before* the
"Enable PLL" writes at the end of the same function. The field is never
written again, and the driver never checks whether the PLL locked.

Because the band search runs while the PLL is still off, it can settle on a
VCO code whose transmit the link partner cannot lock onto: the partner's
system-side SerDes shows no block lock, the USXGMII in-band AN word never
completes, and the lane stays down for good. On at least one W1700K this
reproduces 100% of the time; it is also the likely cause of the "lan2 only
comes up on some boots" reports, where the one-shot search happens to land on
a usable code.

Re-run the search once the PLL is enabled and the lane is fully configured. A
TCLVAR transition while the PLL runs re-triggers it; the final value does not
matter (0x3 and 0x5 both work), only that the field changes with the PLL up.
That has to happen after the whole configuration sequence, so it is wired in
as a post_config op, called at the end of airoha_pcs_config(), and only for
the ETH lane (USXGMII/10GBASER). The PON lane is untouched.

One-line check on a live, unpatched board (ETH-lane pcs_ana + 0x30, TCLVAR is
bits [2:0]):

  devmem 0x1fa7a030                 # 0x0000301B, lane dead
  devmem 0x1fa7a030 32 0x0000301D   # link comes up within ~1-2s

Reported on one board only; the devmem line above is how to confirm it on
another one.

Not merged upstream as of 2026-10-20.

Signed-off-by: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha.h
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha.h
@@ -1260,6 +1260,8 @@
 		       int index, phy_interface_t interface);
 	void (*link_up)(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv, int index);
 	int (*rxlock_workaround)(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv, int index);
+	void (*post_config)(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv,
+			    int index, phy_interface_t interface);
 };
 
 #define to_airoha_pcs_port(n) container_of(n, struct airoha_pcs_port, pcs)
@@ -1274,6 +1276,8 @@
 
 void an7581_pcs_phya_link_up(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv, int index);
 int an7581_pcs_rxlock_workaround(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv, int index);
+void an7581_pcs_jcpll_recal(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv,
+			    int index, phy_interface_t interface);
 #else
 static inline int an7581_pcs_alloc_regmap_fields(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv)
 {
@@ -1307,4 +1311,10 @@
 {
 	return 0;
 }
+
+static inline void an7581_pcs_jcpll_recal(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv,
+					  int index,
+					  phy_interface_t interface)
+{
+}
 #endif
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -659,6 +659,9 @@
 				AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN | AIROHA_PCS_XFI_RX_FC_EN :
 				0);
 
+	if (data->post_config)
+		data->post_config(priv, index, interface);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -1266,6 +1269,7 @@
 	.bringup = an7581_pcs_bringup,
 	.link_up = an7581_pcs_phya_link_up,
 	.rxlock_workaround = an7581_pcs_rxlock_workaround,
+	.post_config = an7581_pcs_jcpll_recal,
 };
 
 static const struct airoha_pcs_match_data an7581_pcs_pon = {
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -1906,6 +1906,27 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+void an7581_pcs_jcpll_recal(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv,
+			    int index, phy_interface_t interface)
+{
+	struct regmap_field **pcs_ana_fields = priv->pcs_ana_fields[index];
+
+	if (interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII &&
+	    interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10GBASER)
+		return;
+
+	/* an7581_pcs_jcpll_bringup() runs the VCO band search with the PLL
+	 * still off, so it can settle on a code the link partner cannot lock
+	 * onto. Transition the field again now that the PLL is up and the
+	 * lane is fully configured: the search re-runs and settles on a
+	 * usable band. The final value does not matter, only that it changed
+	 * while the PLL is running.
+	 */
+	regmap_field_write(pcs_ana_fields[AN7581_PCS_JCPLL_VCO_TCLVAR], 0x3);
+	usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+	regmap_field_write(pcs_ana_fields[AN7581_PCS_JCPLL_VCO_TCLVAR], 0x5);
+}
+
 static void an7581_pcs_pll_bringup(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv,
 				   int index, phy_interface_t interface)
 {
